    <string name="about_fork_title">Fork and credits</string>
    <string name="about_fork_body">Meross Local Pairer is an independent fork of Custom Pairer for Meross Devices, originally created by Alberto Geniola. This fork is maintained by mazkagaz and has substantial changes: Bluetooth LE provisioning for devices that expose it, TLS, local-only login, trusted Wi-Fi handling, device revocation and re-claiming, a simplified setup and a redesigned interface. The MRS100 is the primary test target; other Meross models are welcome, and reports are useful.\n\nAlberto Geniola also wrote the original Meross low-level library and documentation. Icons: Freepik (flaticon.com).</string>
    <string name="about_legal_title">Principles and legal notices</string>
    <string name="about_legal_body">• Not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Meross or the original author. Meross is a trademark of its owner.\n• Local only: no Meross cloud account, no ads, no tracking, no telemetry.\n• Credentials are stored encrypted on the phone. Device names and identifiers stay in your local broker.\n• Open source under GPL-2.0. Provided as is, without warranty. Pairing changes the device configuration; use at your own risk.</string>
    <string name="about_support_title">Open source and support</string>
    <string name="about_support_body">This app is free and open source. If it helps you, you can report issues, suggest improvements or contribute code on GitHub.</string>
    <string name="about_repository_link"><a href="https://github.com/mazkagaz/meross-local-pairer">github.com/mazkagaz/meross-local-pairer</a></string>
    <string name="about_coffee_title">Offer me a coffee</string>
    <string name="about_coffee_subtitle">Optional — the app stays free, open source and ad-free.</string>
